From 635c3ae72bf10acae0066f87785cac366e30c6c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 00:09:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 05/44] feat(chexc): unchecked exceptions and class capturing
 (proposal 6.4, 3.9)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

6.4 unchecked exceptions:
- 'captures'/'throws' clause entries and throw sites consult
  TypeCheckUtil::IsUncheckedExceptionTy (subtype of std.core UncheckedException,
  tolerant of its absence while bootstrapping core).
- Single exemption point in CapabilityCheck::Demand covers throw sites and call
  sites alike, including requirements that instantiate to an unchecked type.
- Proposal 3.2 rule 5: concrete unchecked types are rejected in clauses; type
  parameters stay allowed (their instantiation is exempted instead).

3.9 class capturing (pre-Modal semantics per author rulings 10-12):
- 'captures' EXPERIMENTAL_TOKEN gated by the same flag as 'throws'; clause parsed
  on class and struct headers, reusing the ThrowsClause node; entries validated
  like throws entries; primary constructors rejected on capturing declarations.
- CapabilityCheck: the declaration's own captures supply every member body
  (methods, property accessors, constructors, field initializers) — never the
  superclass's (rule 5); constructor calls demand the constructed declaration's
  captures, instantiated for generic classes, which also covers 'super(...)' and
  delegating 'this(...)' calls.
- Visitors completed for the new field: Collector (clause types collected inside
  the declaration's scope, so they may reference its generic parameters),
  PartialInstantiation, ASTHasher (part of the type's signature hash — it changes
  what constructors demand), plus Walker/Clone/PrintNode.
- ASTKind sizes updated for the six InheritableDecl subtypes.

Gate: CheckedExceptions unchecked 4/4, captures 6/6, parse 11/11, types 10/10,
scopes 7/7 (inference 2/5 red by design, milestone pending); ctest 49/49;
Parser/Sema LLT 3934/3934; clang-format clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
